TITLE:: SPProbe
summary:: the level on any set of busses, and a way to listen to one
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPTree, Classes/SPRouting, Classes/SPMeter

DESCRIPTION::
What link::Classes/SPTree:: measures with. A probe reads audio bus channels at the tail of the root node - after everything that writes them in the block - and answers ten times a second with each one's peak and whether it carried a NaN, an inf or a denormal. Sixteen channels a synth (code::sp_probe16::), as many synths as the list needs and sixteen at most, so a stock server's 64 wire buffers are enough. Control busses are asked for with code::/c_get::.

The probes and the listener are the observer's own synths: SPTree leaves them out of what it shows. Whoever makes a probe frees it.

code::
s.boot;
(
p = SPProbe(s);
p.start;
p.setBusses([0, 1], []);
);
p.level(0);          // nil until the first answer
p.free;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
A probe on a server. Nothing runs until link::#-start::.
ARGUMENT:: server
A link::Classes/Server::.
ARGUMENT:: action
A function called after each batch of answers.

METHOD:: slots
Bus channels a probe synth: 16.

METHOD:: maxSynths
The most probe synths: 16, so 256 channels.

METHOD:: replyRate
Answers a second: 10.

METHOD:: listenOut
The first of the two busses link::#-listen:: plays on: 0.

METHOD:: listenAmp
How loud: 0.5.

METHOD:: isOwn
Whether a SynthDef is a probe's or the listener's.
ARGUMENT:: def
A SynthDef's name.

METHOD:: probeDef
The probe's link::Classes/SynthDef::.

METHOD:: listenDef
The listener's.
ARGUMENT:: channels
1 or 2.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: start
Send the defs and begin. Needs a running server.

METHOD:: stop
Free the synths and stop answering.

METHOD:: free
Stop, and forget every level.

METHOD:: restart
After cmd + period or a reboot: the synths are gone, forget them.

METHOD:: setBusses
The bus channels to measure. More audio channels than fit are left out from the end: put first what matters.
ARGUMENT:: audioIndices
Audio bus channels.
ARGUMENT:: controlIndices
Control bus channels.

METHOD:: audioBusses
The audio channels measured.

METHOD:: level
A channel's peak, held and let fall; nil when it is not measured.
ARGUMENT:: index
An audio bus channel.

METHOD:: raw
The last answer's peak, not held.
ARGUMENT:: index
An audio bus channel.

METHOD:: bad
0 fine, 1 a NaN, 2 an inf, 3 denormals.
ARGUMENT:: index
An audio bus channel.

METHOD:: kval
A control bus's value, after link::#-poll::.
ARGUMENT:: index
A control bus channel.

METHOD:: levelsCopy
Every level now, by channel.

METHOD:: poll
Ask for the control busses' values.

METHOD:: toTail
Move the probes to the end of the root node again, so they read what was written this block.

METHOD:: nodeIDs
The ids of its synths.

METHOD:: listen
Play an audio bus on the outputs, beside whatever plays there. One at a time.
ARGUMENT:: bus
The first channel.
ARGUMENT:: channels
1 or 2.

METHOD:: stopListening
Stop it.

METHOD:: listening
code::[bus, channels]::, or nil.

METHOD:: isListeningTo
Whether that bus is being listened to.
ARGUMENT:: bus
The first channel.

METHOD:: server
Its server.

METHOD:: action
The function called after each batch of answers.
